      "text": "Everything is implemented and error-free. Here's what was built:\n\n**Local-First with Deferred Sync:**\n\n1. **No login required** — the app works exactly as before with all data stored locally in AsyncStorage.\n\n2. **Optional sign-in** — on the Profile tab, there's now an \"Account & Sync\" section at the bottom. If not signed in, it shows a \"Sign in to sync\" card that links to the auth screen.\n\n3. **Auth screen** — a clean modal screen (`/auth`) with email/password sign up and sign in, featuring a mountain backdrop and clear messaging about what sync does.\n\n4. **Automatic data migration** — when a user signs up, all their existing local summit records and custom mountains are uploaded to the cloud. When signing in on a new device, cloud data is pulled and merged with any local data using timestamp-based conflict resolution.\n\n5. **Auto-sync on changes** — whenever summits or custom mountains are saved locally, a debounced cloud push fires automatically if the user is logged in (2-second debounce to avoid excessive writes).\n\n6. **Sync status indicator** — the profile shows a live sync status (Synced/Syncing/Error/Local) with a colored dot, plus a manual \"Sync\" button.\n\n7. **Sign out** — cleanly signs out while keeping all local data intact.",
